## 🔁 Architecture & State Model

### 🧠 Rendering
- **Now**: `next export` creates pre-rendered HTML + JS. No SSR. No dynamic API routes.
- **Later** (Amplify): switch to SSR with server actions, `/api/` routes

### ⚙️ State handling

| Location        | Example                       | State Type        |
|----------------|-------------------------------|-------------------|
| Server-side     | N/A in static mode            | Static JSON/props |
| Client-side     | Contact form, mobile nav      | `useState`, `useRef`, `useForm` (Zod) |
| Shared Config   | `lib/data.ts`                 | Static content    |
| Future SSR      | `lib/api.ts`                  | Fetched at build or runtime via Amplify |

---

## 🧩 Route Responsibilities

| Path               | File                         | Purpose                                                   |
|--------------------|------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| `/`                | `app/page.tsx`               | Home: Hero, divisions overview, CTA                       |
| `/precision-works` | `app/precision-works/page.tsx`| Division: CNC, QA, metrology, 3D printing                |
| `/engineering`     | `app/engineering/page.tsx`    | Division: CFD, FEA, multi-physics                         |
| `/training`        | `app/training/page.tsx`       | Division: CAD, CNC, 3D print training programs            |
| `/about`           | `app/about/page.tsx`          | Company story, mission, leadership                        |
| `/contact`         | `app/contact/page.tsx`        | Static form (to be dynamic later with SES)                |
| `/blog`            | `app/blog/page.tsx`           | Optional MDX articles                                     |

---

## ⚙️ Component Strategy

- Grouped by **page/section**
- Use Tailwind CSS utilities + `shadcn/ui`
- Animate with `framer-motion`
- Every page = fade-in layout with scroll sections

**Example:**
```tsx
<motion.div initial={{opacity: 0}} animate={{opacity: 1}}>
  <SectionTitle title="CNC Machining" />
  <p>We use 3-axis and 5-axis Haas machines...</p>
</motion.div>
🔐 Contact Form (2 Modes)
Now (GitHub Pages):

Uses lib/contact.ts for Zod validation

Submits to Google Forms or custom service (static-only)

Later (AWS Amplify):

Form POSTs to /api/contact/route.ts

Uses AWS SES to send email

Server Action (Next.js + Amplify)

